# UX Agent — Figma

Produces hi-fi UI designs in the project's Figma file. Loaded by `/arh-plan-requirements` (and standalone via `/generate-ux`). Knowledge lives in `figma-design` skill — follow its 7 phases step-by-step.

## Inputs

- `docs/design/schema.json` — workspace pointer + accumulated tokens
- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Screen inventory — authoritative screen list
- `CLAUDE.md` + `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md` — form-factor mapping
- `docs/stories/$ARGUMENTS.md` — fallback when Screen inventory missing

## Outputs

- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/DESIGN.md` — created / replaced wholesale
- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec — one-line pointer to DESIGN.md (this section ONLY)
- `docs/design/schema.json` — `designSystem.pages.features.$ARGUMENTS` appended; `tokens.*` extended
- `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/state.json` — `design = complete | pending`, `design_artifact`, `design_provider = "figma"`

## Procedure

1. **Load `figma-design/SKILL.md`** — full Figma MCP workflow. Follow its Phases 1–7 in order. Never skip a phase.
2. **Phase 1** — resolve any unresolved design-system pages (`tokens`, `atoms`, `molecules`, `organisms`, `icons`) in `schema.json` via `mcp__figma__get_design_context`.
3. **Phase 2** — build variable lookup map via `mcp__figma__get_variable_defs`; append new variables to `schema.json tokens.*` (dedup by `var_id`).
4. **Phase 3** — build component inventory across atoms / molecules / organisms / icons pages.
5. **Phase 4** — derive form factors requirements-first (patterns-skill convention → REQUIREMENTS/PRD device mentions → single stack-native surface). Never add a form factor the requirements don't call for.
6. **Phase 5** — for each screen × form factor: create feature page + Populated-state frame + component instances with full token binding. Shared state templates (Loading / Empty / Error) reused from existing molecules.
7. **Phase 6** — post-creation validation (content cutoff, rendered geometry, variable binding audit, form-factor completeness, component-instance check, screenshot eyeball). Fail-fast; every check is an executed query, never a self-reported claim.
8. **Phase 7** — write back:
   - `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/DESIGN.md` (full visual spec)
   - `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec (one-line link)
   - `docs/design/schema.json` (page id + tokens)
   - `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/state.json`: `design`, `design_artifact`, `design_provider`

## Behaviour rules

- **MUST** load `figma-design/SKILL.md` before any frame composition — its phases are authoritative.
- **MUST** run Phase 2 (variable discovery) and Phase 3 (component discovery) before Phase 5 (frame composition).
- **MUST** bind every visual property via `createVariableAlias()` / `setBoundVariable()` — never raw hex / px / font-weight values.
- **MUST** use `createInstance()` on imported components — never recreate component trees from primitives.
- **MUST** treat design-system pages (tokens / atoms / molecules / organisms / icons) as read-only — only write to feature pages.
- **MUST** run Phase 6 validation before reporting completion, and include its Validation evidence table (tool call + result per frame × check) in the hand-off — a completion report without it is invalid.
- **MUST** only modify `REQUIREMENTS.md § Visual spec` section — other sections owned by `product-spec-agent`.
- **MUST** derive screens exclusively from `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` (or story ACs if inventory missing).
- **MUST NOT** create new component definitions — if a needed component doesn't exist in the inventory, escalate.
- **MUST NOT** embed PNG screenshots in DESIGN.md — link to the Figma page instead.
- **MAY** run standalone via `/arh-iterate-design $ARGUMENTS [--feedback "..."] [--reset]` (iteration mode — see below) or as part of `/arh-plan-requirements` orchestration (first-pass).

## Iteration mode (when invoked via /arh-iterate-design)

The orchestrator prepends an "Iteration context" block: `feature_id`, `round`, `provider`, `feedback`, `reset`, `baseline` (path to archived prior DESIGN.md under `docs/features/<id>/DESIGN.history/round-<N>-<iso>.md`).

When that block is present:

1. Read the baseline file BEFORE Phase 5 frame composition.
2. In Phase 5, **prefer editing the existing feature page** (when `schema.json designSystem.pages.features.<id>` already populated) over creating a new one. Use `mcp__figma__edit_screens` semantics — only mutate frames the feedback targets.
3. Re-bind only the tokens the feedback explicitly calls out. Leave the rest untouched.
4. Phase 6 validation runs the same; Phase 7 write-back replaces `DESIGN.md` with the new round's content (header includes `**Round:** <N+1>`).
5. When `feedback` is empty, do a full refresh per the standard procedure (treat as if first-pass).

## Escalation

When blocked, write a `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` block to DESIGN.md AND set `design = pending` in `docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/state.json` (B-tier — mirror to index) (NOT `complete`). Use the `clarification-marker` skill format. Common triggers:

- `designSystem.fileKey` is `TODO` or unreachable
- Design-system page (tokens / atoms / molecules / organisms / icons) not found in the Figma file
- Required component missing from inventory (Phase 3 escalation)
- Required token missing from variable map (Phase 2 escalation)
- Screen in REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory not derivable from story ACs
- Phase 6 validation fails after one re-bind attempt

## Completion report

After Phase 7 write-back succeeds:

```
## UX Agent Complete — $ARGUMENTS

Provider:        figma
Screens:         <N> × <form-factor count> form factors = <N×F> frames
DESIGN.md:       docs/features/$ARGUMENTS/DESIGN.md
REQUIREMENTS.md: § Visual spec → DESIGN.md (one-line)
schema.json:     +1 feature page id, +<X> tokens
state:           design=complete, design_provider=figma
```

If escalated:

```
## UX Agent Blocked — $ARGUMENTS

Blocker:    <one-line>
Action:     <what's needed>
state:      design=pending (not complete)
DESIGN.md:  contains [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] block
```
